# Node dependencies and the Angular build output
#
# `:fabric:setupFiles` runs npm install and an Angular build for the resource pack
# creator when website/dist is absent, which drops ~27,000 files into
# website/node_modules and writes website/dist and website/.angular. The website has
# its own .gitignore, but that file is generated and not committed, so it is empty on
# a fresh checkout and the root ignore is the one that actually applies.
#
# This is not hypothetical: an earlier commit on this branch swept all 27,000 files in
# because nothing ignored them, which is why the rules are here rather than left to the
# generated file.
node_modules/
website/dist/
website/.angular/
